From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:07:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1275/3799] soh: rename func_80042708 ->
 CollisionPoly_GetPointOnIntersectLine

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: its doc comment reads "Gets the closestPoint to point on the line formed from the intersection of planes polyA and polyB"; it is a thin wrapper over Math3D_PlaneVsPlaneVsLineClosestPoint.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/include/functions.h  | 2 +-
 soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/include/functions.h b/soh/include/functions.h
index bda6aa7c3..7392411e4 100644
--- a/soh/include/functions.h
+++ b/soh/include/functions.h
@@ -712,7 +712,7 @@ s32 WaterBox_GetSurfaceImpl(PlayState* play, CollisionContext* colCtx, f32 x, f3
 u32 WaterBox_GetCamDataIndex(CollisionContext* colCtx, WaterBox* waterBox);
 u16 WaterBox_GetCameraSType(CollisionContext* colCtx, WaterBox* waterBox);
 u32 WaterBox_GetLightSettingIndex(CollisionContext* colCtx, WaterBox* waterBox);
-s32 func_80042708(CollisionPoly* polyA, CollisionPoly* polyB, Vec3f* point, Vec3f* closestPoint);
+s32 CollisionPoly_GetPointOnIntersectLine(CollisionPoly* polyA, CollisionPoly* polyB, Vec3f* point, Vec3f* closestPoint);  // was func_80042708 [LLM:HIGH]
 s32 func_800427B4(CollisionPoly* polyA, CollisionPoly* polyB, Vec3f* pointA, Vec3f* pointB, Vec3f* closestPoint);
 void BgCheck_DrawDynaCollision(PlayState*, CollisionContext*);
 void BgCheck_DrawStaticCollision(PlayState*, CollisionContext*);
diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c b/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
index 389a71afd..89e55fb64 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_bgcheck.c
@@ -4384,7 +4384,8 @@ s32 func_800425B0(PlayState* play, CollisionContext* colCtx, f32 x, f32 z, f32*
  * Gets the `closestPoint` to `point` on the line formed from the intesection of planes `polyA` and `polyB`
  * returns true if the `closestPoint` exists, else returns false
  */
-s32 func_80042708(CollisionPoly* polyA, CollisionPoly* polyB, Vec3f* point, Vec3f* closestPoint) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80042708: its doc comment reads "Gets the closestPoint to point on the line formed from the intersection of planes polyA and polyB"; it is a thin wrapper over Math3D_PlaneVsPlaneVsLineClosestPoint.
+s32 CollisionPoly_GetPointOnIntersectLine(CollisionPoly* polyA, CollisionPoly* polyB, Vec3f* point, Vec3f* closestPoint) {
     f32 n1X;
     f32 n1Y;
     f32 n1Z;
